Description: add top-level makefile and legacy include-prefix shims
 Upstream runs make in bepdf/ and xpdf/ as two separate projects; the
 vos_makefile_engine buildsystem invokes make once at the source root.
 Add a top-level generic makefile that drives both source sets through
 one engine invocation (viewer + bundled xpdf-derived sources merged
 into a single link), plus voscompat/ shims: forwarding headers for the
 legacy be/ include prefix, which the packaged headers do not ship, and
 redirects for the two bundled header names (UTF8.h, Catalog.h) that
 the packaged headers also ship. A locales symlink at the source root
 points at bepdf/locales, where upstream keeps the translation
 sources, so the buildsystem's catalog step finds them. The separate
 columnlistview link entry is dropped because that library's classes
 are exported by libbe here, and -std=gnu++11 is forced because the
 bundled xpdf-derived code uses dynamic exception specifications that
 newer dialects removed (gnu++11 is the V\OS tree default). CFLAGS
 opens with voscompat and the packaged real header root so the legacy
 and <os/...>/<private/...> include styles resolve to the intended
 headers ahead of the redirect wrappers that the spec file's -I
 ordering would otherwise pick.
Author: Numerio <b.vitruvio@gmail.com>
Forwarded: no
Origin: https://github.com/HaikuArchives/BePDF

